    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0709" n="1443" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1443"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-01-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                    1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Instructions in telegram of 2d anticipated and executed. Nine hundred just killed
                    between Ourfa and Aintab. Road is not safe for Miss Shattuck, who wires she is
                    well, but distressed. Porte declares missionary <pb facs="0710" n="1444"
                        xml:id="pg1444"/> statement that soldiers pillaged boarding school at Marash
                    to be calumny, and says missionaries sent address of thanks for protection there
                    afforded. It may have been sent, for the poor men were in fearful duress.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
